# Project Configuration

> This file is read by agents and pipeline scripts.
> Fill in the values below before running the pipeline.
> Lives at `.tlk/PROJECT.md` so the project root stays clean.

## Project-Specific Configuration

- **Test command:** `<your test command, e.g. npm test or pytest>`
- **Focused test command:** `<optional: run a subset, e.g. npm test -- or pytest — Cmok appends a path/pattern. Leave as a placeholder to have Cmok filter the test command itself.>`
- **Build command:** `<your build command, e.g. npm run build or make>`
- **Version files:** `<comma-separated list of files to version-bump, or "none", e.g. package.json, manifest.json>`
- **Artifacts directory:** `.tlk/`
- **Design system directory:** `design-system/`
- **Judge command:** `<optional: CLI for LLM-as-judge in autoresearch loop. Defaults to `claude -p --allowedTools none`. Set to e.g. `gemini -p` to swap providers.>`
- **Pace thresholds:** `<optional: override usage-limit pace rules, e.g. slow5h=-15 slow7d=-10 push5h=20 push7d=10 stop5h=90 stop7d=95 — any subset. Read by talaka/statusline/tools/pace.sh and the statusline.>`

> **Test command vs Focused test command.** Bagnik's gate always runs the full **Test command** — it is the only worker that can say regression is green. Cmok runs only the tests covering what it changed: the **Focused test command** if you set one, otherwise it filters the test command itself. Keep both values as bare commands with no trailing prose — scripts read them by stripping the label and executing the rest.

